{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Cain said</b>. The near [meaning] is that he said to him all the reproofs that HaShem had reproved. And questioners born on a cloudy day will ask how he struck him, when there was no sword — and this is a void question, for he could kill him with his hand by strangulation, and a thousand [means of] wood and stone are available,"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:07.114845862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}